  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "section-introduction",
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "sourceAnchor": "introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n\tThe Dragonscarred feat provides a permanent damage resistance and a fantastic\n\timprovement to the Dragon’s Fear feature from the Cult of the Dragon Initiate\n\tfeat. However, the ability score increase doesn’t let you improve the DC of\n\tDragon’s Fear, which is extremely frustrating.\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n\tBecause the ability scores don’t line up, anyone hoping to capitalize on\n\tDragon’s Fear may need to accept that their save DC won’t be maximized.\n\tConquest Paladins are still a great candidate, but a Charisma-based build may\n\tbe your best choice unless you’re happy to let your Strength/Dexterity fall\n\tbehind for a while.\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n\tDragonscarred requires\n\t"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n\t\t"
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Cult of the Dragon Initiate",
              "href": "https://www.google.com/url?q=https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/feats/cult-of-the-dragon-initiate/&sa=D&source=editors&ust=1762230330141551&usg=AOvVaw1PSkD4_HIBJikIzVvhb9pD"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n\t"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n\t.\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-ability-score-increase",
      "heading": "Ability Score Increase",
      "sourceAnchor": "ability-score-increase",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-ability-score-increase-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n\tCult of the Dragon Initiate’s Dragon’s Fear feature has a Wisdom-based DC, but\n\tthis feat lets you choose to increase either Wisdom or Charisma. Why?\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-ability-score-increase-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n\tThe Dragon Cultist Background lets you increase Dex, Con, or Int. Cult of the\n\tDragon Initate has a Wisdom-based DC. Dragonscarred lets you increase Con or\n\tCharisma. WHY? Who thought this was a good idea?\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-ability-score-increase-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Dragonscarred requires "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Cult of the Dragon Initiate",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/feats/cult-of-the-dragon-initiate/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-damage-resistance",
      "heading": "Damage Resistance",
      "sourceAnchor": "damage-resistance",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-damage-resistance-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n\tA permanent damage resistance is great, but strongly consider Gift of the\n\tChromatic Dragon if you’re just here for the damage resistance.\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-fearsome-power",
      "heading": "Fearsome Power",
      "sourceAnchor": "fearsome-power",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-fearsome-power-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n\tA massive improvement to Dragon’s Fear. If your build doesn’t already lean on\n\tyour Bonus Action heavily, you may be able to use it every turn.\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
